notes.body:
Without having to do the separate `proto_item_append_text` call.

You could re-used the value string for the parameters of the same width. I forget how well negative numbers + different widths are handled, but it's possible that you even get away with something like:

```
static const value_string sd_specialvals[] = {
    {-1,    "ANY"},
    {0, NULL}
};
```

and it would actually work for all of them, so long as you marked the type. (I'd have to check on all the casts and sign extensions of the different widths, though.)

